      "tree_id": "11c0601f39e4acb2abd4e0469c83e2b9fd9a6f5a",
      "message": "Integer factoring 1/2: closed upstream rerun profile for 1337isnot1337's claimed proof (Lean v4.33.1)\n\nLead decision 2026-10-30, option A. The trusted challenge is Rudich and Rousseau's Challenge.lean\n(c91cc3f4, blob 6d9bf51d) byte for byte, plus one appended theorem:\nIntegerFactoring.HalfAppendix.sqrtLogLog_factoring : Factoring.SqrtLogLogConjecture, that is time\nC * 2^(C*n/(sqrt(log2 n)+1)), score 1/2. It has the name of the claimed proof, so their commit\ne91442d3 is checked as it is; no repackaging is needed. A test pins the prefix to the frozen file.\n\nThe proof's import closure (574 modules, read statically) comes from four pinned sources: their\nformal-appendix (91 roots, solution module HalfTheorem) and formal (HalfPad, HalfPrefix) at\ne91442d3, Rudich c91cc3f4 (Challenge, FactoringAux), and anthropics/formal-math 16a5ce41 (six\neth/proof folders). Lean v4.33.1 with profiles/anthropic-lake-manifest.json (same package revisions\nas eth's manifest, Mathlib 0df444a) and anthropic-tools.json. auto_implicit true, as their builds.\n\nVerifier change: a solution dependency may give lean_options. The generated lakefile writes them as\n[lean_lib.leanOptions] on that dependency's roots (Lake applies a library's options after the\npackage's). The eth folders get their lakefile's options (autoImplicit false, relaxedAutoImplicit\nfalse, exponentiation.threshold 2048, pp.unicode.fun true). Only booleans and non-negative integers\nare accepted. Every existing profile gets a byte-identical lakefile (checked against the old function\nfor all 10, and by a test).\n\nAn offline run of prepare() on the real downloaded trees (nothing built) staged 654 files and\nplanned the 574 modules with no collision. Closed: no direct.json entry; only a maintainer dispatch\nof verify.yml runs it. No Lean ran on any of our machines. Tests: tests/test_integer_factoring_sqrtlog.py;\n207 pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
